  "paragraph": 10,
  "text": "Here is the crucial detail that demystifies tool calling completely: the language model never runs code or touches your disk itself. Instead, the harness passes JSON tool schemas along with the API request, describing what functions exist and what arguments they take. When the model wants to inspect auth.ts, it simply outputs a structured JSON tool call with a unique call ID. Your harness parses that payload, executes the real read function on the machine, and appends a paired tool result message matching that exact ID back into the conversation.",
